# Box art drive for the landing-page games carousel (site/demos/box-art.mjs).
# Format: <frame:int> <KeyName> <down|up>; frames advance by --script-dt, and
# tetris moves on key DOWN edges, so each action is a down/up pair.
#
# One piece every 20 frames: rotate, shuffle it a few columns off centre, then
# hard-drop (Space). The column offsets cycle over the whole board so the stack
# grows flat-ish and keeps clearing rows instead of topping out. Long enough to
# cover the captured window (frames 300-474).
#
#   functor -d examples/tetris run native --input-script boxart.script \
#     --script-dt 0.0166667 --capture-at-frame 300 --capture-frame /tmp/tetris.png

